{
  "dom_id": "step-q112065",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14218944/assets/750ef4e4dc4c70ccbd9f7b30ca7c15e996535d55daf95e6eeeaaf3f096b3cf15.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following is the graph of $y=f(\\frac{1}{5}x)?$\n\n(*Note: Figures not drawn to scale*)",
  "worked_solution": "To graph the function $y=f(\\frac{1}{5}x),$ we take the graph of $y=f(x)$ and stretch it by factor of $5$ parallel to the $x$-axis. This has the effect of multiplying the $x$-coordinates of all points on $y=f(x)$ by $5.$\n\nThe resulting graph is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14218944/assets/8fb2bcfc545d9a6b9cf316b758d82a96c8807169ab345cb3cf8cce03d456c50e.png)",
